{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502066-how-do-avatars-effect-the-game-mechanics","id":1502066,"title":"how do avatars effect the game mechanics?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-03T17:42:07-08:00","id":1502066,"title":"how do avatars effect the game mechanics?","content":"how do avatars shape how you use magic, mechanics wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T17:48:12-08:00","id":1502068,"title":"","content":"Entirely depends on the ST. They're characters of their own and while you will design them, it will depend on the ST how much they come to the fore and how much they shape the Mage and his choices. Some will be friends along the way, others will be a thing in the corner of your mind and third will be harsh mistresses. What this actually means is that they don't play by the same rules a PC does.<br /> <br /> Essentially the Avatar is a part of who you are and where you need to be. Whatever the Avatar is, it's something that resonates with the Character even if they don't understand yet why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T17:49:36-08:00","id":1502069,"title":"","content":"They don't really. You need to have an Avatar (or a piece of one shoved in a Wonder) to cast awakened magic.<br /> <br /> Your connection to your Avatar (as measured by the Background) lets you store more Quintessence and spend more of it at once.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, Avatars are less mechanical and more narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T05:48:34-08:00","id":1502198,"title":"","content":"Your relationship with your avatar can impact how easy magic is to cast, with a bad relationship manifesting as a +1 to +3 to difficulty.<br /> <br /> if your mage is constantly shirking the lessons their avatar is guiding them towards or engaging in magic they do not approve of, the. That is when this penalty can come in to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T20:24:00-08:00","id":1502279,"title":"","content":"How about some narrative tips and examples on how to make Avatars interesting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T05:12:46-08:00","id":1502298,"title":"","content":"The effects of the Avatar are about as mechanical as you want to make them. As a baseline, that's as Heavy Arms described; though Saikou's point is also a thing if the Storyteller wants to go there. In particular, though, Saikou's point <i>also</i> gives some indications of what the relationship <i>isn't: </i>it isn't one where the Avatar has the ability to deny the mage access to her magick. The Avatar can guide; but it can't dictate. That said, if you <i>want </i>that sort of relationship between your mage and her Avatar, it's trivial to adapt the Faithless Flaw to that purpose.<br /> <br /> There are also the Seekings, which are arguably the primary role that the Avatar plays in a mage's life: whenever you go to raise your Arete, you go through a Seeking where your Avatar challenges you: pass the challenge, and your Arete increases; fail, and you need to do more before you can try again.<br /> <br /> And the Resonance mechanics can be tied to your Avatar, too. Ultimately, the kind of Resonance a mage acquires depends on the actions of that mage; where the Avatar factors in its in what kinds of actions it tries to encourage. Each Avatar Essence has a corresponding type of Resonance that its guidance tends to lead the mage to acquire if she follows it: a Questing Avatar tends to promote Devotional Resonance; a Primordial Avatar tends to promote Elemental Resonance; a Pattern Avatar tends to promote Stabilizing Resonance; and a Dynamic Avatar tends to promote Temperamental Resonance. And conversely, the Resonance that the mage develops can influence the nature of the Avatar: not so much as to change the Avatar's Essence; but if you develop, say, Vindictive Resonance, your Avatar should start to take on more a more vindictive tone.<br /> <br /> Finally, MRev introduced some Avatar-related Merits and Flaws that can lead to radically different relationships between mages and their Avatars. I personally make Circumspect Avatar the default for technomancers, free of charge; their Avatars/Geniuses tend to sit quietly in the background hardly ever interfering and rarely doing so in ways that the mage will recognize as a guiding hand on their life. Manifest Avatars, on the other hand, are extremely active in the mage's life, to the point that you can also take your Avatar as an Ally and it will become a sort of invisible companion in the mage's stories, even able to physically manifest and take action on its own. Toss in the Phylactery Flaw, and your Avatar <i>has</i> a physical form of its own \u2014 which can be destroyed, with catastrophic consequences for the mage. And those aren't the only options, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-06-2023, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}